WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
World Models are turning old Pokemon Go scans into training grounds for robots. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 221. Diwali stickers from your own photos, notes on new art tools and a privacy prompt, then a weekend review. Niantic, the company behind Pokemon Go sold that game last year, wired reports, and now builds three-dimensional digital replicas of real places from its collection of environment data. Three-dimensional means the copy has height, width, and depth.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.580
Like a street you could actually walk through. Picture a dusk walk in 2016 with

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.940
your phone out to catch a snorlax. The app scanned the buildings and streets while

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:45.040
hundreds of millions of players did the same thing. That pile of scenery is now fuel for

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.980
a new kind of artificial intelligence system, or AI. A world model looks at visual inputs

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:56.480
like photos or video frames. It then predicts the next visual state of a scene, including

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:02.120
physics which just means the rules of how things move. It tries to get falling objects and

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:07.320
swinging doors to behave the way they do in real life. Brian McClendon is the Chief Technology

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.760
Officer at Niantic Spatial, the person who leads the tech there. He wants to reconstruct

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.340
the real world in software so robots can rehearse inside safe digital copies instead of the physical

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:24.600
room. Treat those copies like a practice gym that matches your actual street. The robot can stumble,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.500
travel, retry, and learn without scraping a real wall.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.740
A few photos of a kitchen or hallway can unlock millions of practice sessions for that robot.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.160
It is like handing a student two textbook pages and then letting them drill millions

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.440
of practice problems.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.100
Driverless cars use the same trick to learn split-second reactions to obstacles without ever

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:44.980
leaving a computer.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.300
That is the same idea as a flight simulator that trains a pilot before anyone leaves the ground.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:56.900
more reliable home robots could follow by 2027, even if you never open the software yourself.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.640
Safe or self-driving cars, also called autonomous vehicles, could follow on that same timeline.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.620
Artists and game designers may also build virtual spaces from ordinary photos

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.020
like dropping snapshots into Minecraft and watching a walkable world grow.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.140
There is no public demo yet that lets you run full physics simulations.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.120
options. You can still try the core idea in two dimensions, meaning a flat picture instead

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:27.480
of a walkable copy. Open chat GPT or the Gemini app, upload a photo of a room, and ask

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.740
it to show the scene after a small change, like a door swinging open. Watch whether the

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.900
new picture still respects gravity and hinges. Your phone keyboard watches the words you

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.800
just wrote and takes a guess at the next one. All over Cameron, Chief Executive Officer

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.580
of the AI lab Odyssey puts the difference in that same shape.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.460
A language model is an AI that predicts the next word in a sentence.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.480
A world model predicts the next image after it sees the current one.

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:56.926
Show it one photo of a kitchen.

00:02:57.526 --> 00:03:01.286
It tries to guess the next picture if a chair slides or a covered door moves.

00:03:01.886 --> 00:03:06.606
It picks up those rules the way you learn that a ball rolls downhill by seeing the pattern

00:03:06.606 --> 00:03:07.406
again and again.

00:03:07.406 --> 00:03:12.386
Think of a flip book, each page is a guess at the frame that should come after the last

00:03:12.386 --> 00:03:12.746
one.

00:03:13.086 --> 00:03:17.406
The model plays that guessing game on huge piles of examples until the next picture

00:03:17.406 --> 00:03:18.426
looks physically right.

00:03:19.106 --> 00:03:23.066
A robot can then rehearse walking through a kitchen it has never physically visited,

00:03:23.506 --> 00:03:26.666
because the model already expects what happens if it bumps a chair.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:31.226
All of that rehearsal stays inside the computer, so no real mug gets smashed.

00:03:31.946 --> 00:03:34.786
Later the robot carries those lessons into the actual room.

00:03:35.286 --> 00:03:36.586
You now hold the whole trick.

00:03:36.586 --> 00:03:40.766
It is next-picture guessing with falling and swinging baked into the guests.

00:03:41.996 --> 00:03:47.356
Chat GPT and Gemini, live mint notes, can take a regular selfie and add traditional outfits,

00:03:47.816 --> 00:03:52.116
Diaz, Rangoli, and warm lighting while keeping your face exactly the same.

00:03:52.776 --> 00:03:57.736
It is a festive shortcut for Diwali greetings, like borrowing a costume department that still

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:58.856
draws your real face.

00:03:59.436 --> 00:04:01.856
Anyone with a phone can try this in under two minutes.

00:04:01.856 --> 00:04:07.736
Open Chat GPT or the Gemini app, upload a clear photo of yourself, and paste a prompt

00:04:07.736 --> 00:04:08.396
like this.

00:04:08.816 --> 00:04:14.036
Turn this photograph into a cute, high-quality WhatsApp sticker for Diwali 2026.

00:04:14.576 --> 00:04:16.476
Keep my original face and skin tone.

00:04:17.096 --> 00:04:20.436
Add a traditional outfit and a small deal with a transparent background.

00:04:21.096 --> 00:04:25.056
WhatsApp is the messaging app where you can send that sticker straight to friends and family.

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:27.216
The same idea works in Gemini.

00:04:27.716 --> 00:04:29.956
Just describe the outfit and background you want.

00:04:29.956 --> 00:04:34.776
then download the result. For more control, name a sorry or shawani,

00:04:35.336 --> 00:04:40.076
merry gold flowers, fairy lights, or cinematic lighting. Always remind the tool

00:04:40.076 --> 00:04:43.496
to preserve your original facial features and natural skin texture.

00:04:44.176 --> 00:04:48.176
Both tools work on phones and computers and the pictures are ready to share as

00:04:48.176 --> 00:04:52.956
stickers or greeting images. Try two prompts in a row and notice which details

00:04:52.956 --> 00:04:57.916
stay locked to your real face. The manga artist behind Vinland Saga in a

00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:01.696
discussion on Reddit publicly shared support for AI-generated art.

00:05:02.276 --> 00:05:07.176
Even an established creator is pointing at value in the new tools, sitting them alongside

00:05:07.176 --> 00:05:09.876
traditional art instead of treating them as a replacement.

00:05:10.456 --> 00:05:12.656
More like a new brush left next to the pencils.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.600
A trending chat GPT prompt.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.640
Be in crypto warns turns your chat history into a visual room.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:23.940
It is fun to try, like building a tiny museum of your old conversations.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
Posting that picture publicly can accidentally share personal details that scammers might use.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.900
Check what you are comfortable showing before you send it anywhere.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.180
The way you would close a diary before leaving it on a table.

00:05:37.221 --> 00:05:41.421
Old game scans were not the only thing shifting under you across the last seven days.

00:05:41.921 --> 00:05:45.821
So here is where chat GPT and the wider tools stood by the end of the week.

00:05:46.361 --> 00:05:50.761
Open AI is folding its separate work mode back into regular chat GPT

00:05:50.761 --> 00:05:53.741
and your usage limits are about to share one pool.

00:05:54.321 --> 00:05:56.821
Chat GPT now handles one in five searches

00:05:56.821 --> 00:05:58.341
that used to go straight to Google.

00:05:58.861 --> 00:06:01.141
A new study found AI already handles up

00:06:01.141 --> 00:06:02.681
to half the work scientists do

00:06:02.681 --> 00:06:04.501
when running real research projects.

